  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.06t & =-6.6 \\\\ 100\\cdot (-0.06t) & =100\\cdot (-6.6) \\\\ -6t & =-660\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-6$ to isolate $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6t & =-660 \\\\ \\frac{-6t}{-6} & =\\frac{-660}{-6} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-6}t}{\\cancel{-6}} & =110 \\\\ t & =110\\end{aligned}\n$$",
